# Best-model trackers
*_best.txt

# Claude Code
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately TRACKED. It is the contract this repo is worked
# under, so it has to travel with a clone and be reviewable in a diff.
.claude/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Blender walker assets (make_walker.py / make_walker_scene.py): the machine
# and the final frames are tracked, but the scene file and the review passes
# are regenerable output — rebuild with
#   make_walker_scene.py -- --shot hero --no-render     (scene.blend)
#   make_walker.py -- --stage build --render            (clay/)
# Patterns are callsign-agnostic because the output directory is derived from
# CALLSIGN, so --callsign ONYX writes assets/onyx/ and stays ignored too.
assets/*/scene.blend
assets/*/clay/
assets/*/blockout_spec/
assets/*/blockout_crouch/

# MuJoCo writes this next to the cwd on any GL/context failure.
MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Fixture trees for the check_* oracles. Removed in a finally block, so these
# only survive a hard kill mid-test.
.tmp_check_checkpoint_width/
.tmp_check_retire/

# core.hooksPath points git at .githooks/, so that directory is tracked and
# ships with a clone. That is right for pre-push and wrong for this one file:
# it enforces a local commit-message convention, which is a property of this
# working copy rather than of the project, so it is installed per-machine and
# not carried to anyone else's clone.
.githooks/prepare-commit-msg

# Isaac Lab / Newton viewer runtime state. The imgui window layout is written
# into the CWD on exit, so it appears wherever a viewer was launched from.
imgui.ini

# Isaac Lab's MjcfConverter bookkeeping, written beside the USD it produces.
# `config.yaml` records the ABSOLUTE input path on the machine that ran the
# conversion and `.asset_hash` keys the laziness check against it, so both are
# properties of one working copy rather than of the project — committing them
# would put this machine's home directory in a public repo and would make a
# clone elsewhere trust a hash it cannot reproduce. The generated MJCF and the
# USD tree next to them ARE tracked; regenerate with
#   PYTHONPATH=src ~/IsaacLab/isaaclab.sh -p -m bestiary.isaac.hound_usd
assets/*/isaac/config.yaml
assets/*/isaac/.asset_hash
